.TH BTRFS-BACKUPCTL 1 "September 2026" "btrfs-backup 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btrfs-backupctl \- configure, inspect and recover btrfs-backup repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btrfs-backupctl
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B btrfs-backupctl
provides profile configuration, status, repository maintenance, backup
planning, target control and transactional restore commands. Commands that
change system configuration or target state require the permissions enforced
by the caller's environment or the system manager.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --status-root " PATH"
Override the status root.
.TP
.BI --history-root " PATH"
Override the history root.
.TP
.BI --profile-dir " PATH"
Override the profile configuration root.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command help.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B profile
List, create, validate, render, save, regenerate, show or export profiles. The
.B wizard
subcommand guides interactive configuration.
.TP
.B repository rebuild
Inspect a repository catalog rebuild, or commit it with
.BR --apply .
.TP
.B status
Show current status, read history, or watch for status changes.
.TP
.B installation
Render or validate systemd and udev installation artifacts.
.TP
.B runner
Plan, execute or cancel a backup run. Machine-readable output is written to
standard output.
.TP
.B restore
Inspect a catalog, list snapshot contents and versions, preview a restore,
execute it, or perform a restore drill. Restore execution stages content and
publishes only a complete result.
.TP
.B target
Activate, deactivate, mount or eject the configured target.
.TP
.B upgrade preflight
Check whether installed profile documents satisfy the current schema.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
btrfs-backupctl status show --all --human
btrfs-backupctl runner plan --profile default --offline
btrfs-backupctl target mount --profile default
btrfs-backupctl restore catalog --repository /mnt/backup/btrfs-backup
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command returns zero on success, one for an operational failure where the
subcommand defines that distinction, and two for invalid input or usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btrfs-backup (8),
.BR btrfs (8),
.BR cryptsetup (8)
